    "summary": "High‑energy San Diego show with epic Truckin'→Other One→Eyes jam",
    "blurb": "The second set rolls through a blistering Truckin' → The Other One → Eyes of the World sandwich and a soaring Wharf Rat coda. Jerry’s lead work shines on Here Comes Sunshine and China Cat > Rider, while Keith’s piano adds texture throughout. Soundboard recordings capture the performance with crystal‑clear detail.",
    "review": "The November 14, 1973 San Diego Sports Arena gig finds the Dead firing on all cylinders. The first set offers solid staples—Sugaree, Here Comes Sunshine (despite a tiny ending slip), and a bright China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider that hints at the fireworks to come. The real highlight erupts in the second set: Truckin' launches into a multi‑reprise Other One sandwich that feeds directly into an expansive Eyes of the World, before resolving with a heartfelt Wharf Rat coda. Keith’s piano swells and wanes with wah‑inflected flair, Bill Kreutzmann keeps the groove loose yet propulsive, and Phil’s bass bombs drive the jams forward. Jerry’s guitar is both tight and adventurous, delivering scorching leads on Sunshine and inventive noodling throughout. The setlist flows naturally, and the energy stays high from opening to the final One More Saturday Night. Among the available sources, Charlie Miller’s soundboard transfer (gd1973-11-14.sbd.miller.79049.flac16) offers the clearest, most balanced portrait of this memorable night.",
